sure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133522296,imgsize-145787.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump sends Saudi nuclear deal to Congress, keeps Israel normalisation as condition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133529810.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The United States has submitted a civil nuclear cooperation agreement with Saudi Arabia to Congress. This pact will only proceed if Riyadh agrees to normalize relations with Israel. Congress has ninety days to review the proposed thirty-year agreement for potential nuclear proliferation concerns. The deal facilitates US companies' involvement in Saudi Arabia's nuclear program development. Saudi Arabia's stance on Palestinian statehood remains a significant hurdle for normalization.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trump-sends-saudi-civil-nuclear-deal-to-congress-keeps-israel-normalisation-as-condition/articleshow/133529810.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trump-sends-saudi-civil-nuclear-deal-to-congress-keeps-israel-normalisation-as-condition/articleshow/133529810.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T10:16:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133529903,imgsize-142534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scottish town raises £6 million to create a vast 10,500-acre nature reserve]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133529619.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-small-scottish-town-raised-6-million-to-buy-10500-acres-from-a-major-landowner-its-new-nature-reserve-is-now-restoring-190-hectares-of-degraded-peatland/articleshow/133529619.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-small-scottish-town-raised-6-million-to-buy-10500-acres-from-a-major-landowner-its-new-nature-reserve-is-now-restoring-190-hectares-of-degraded-peatland/articleshow/133529619.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T10:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133529836,imgsize-1725604.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kentucky golf course shut after low turnout is becoming a 225-acre park, 70% greenspace]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133523448.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Kentucky county closed its 225-acre Fox Run Golf Course after it averaged just 9,000 to 10,000 rounds annually. Now, the former golf property is being transformed into a major public park featuring trails, climbing areas, biking facilities, water features and family spaces. Around 70% of the site will remain preserved as natural greenspace for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-county-closed-a-225-acre-golf-course-after-it-averaged-only-9000-to-10000-rounds-a-year-the-site-is-now-becoming-one-of-the-countys-largest-new-public-parks-with-70-preserved-as-greenspace/articleshow/133523448.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-county-closed-a-225-acre-golf-course-after-it-averaged-only-9000-to-10000-rounds-a-year-the-site-is-now-becoming-one-of-the-countys-largest-new-public-parks-with-70-preserved-as-greenspace/articleshow/133523448.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T01:24:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133523491,imgsize-277149.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wiltshire couple face demolition of home they built for disabled daughter in 2022 after planning row]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133526561.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Wiltshire couple who built a four-bedroom home for their disabled daughter in 2022 now face a council demolition order following a planning dispute. The property, built on Green Belt land, includes a basement and decking that were not part of the approved plans. The couple have appealed to the Planning Inspectorate, with a decision expected in autumn.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-couple-built-a-four-bedroom-home-in-wiltshire-for-their-disabled-daughter-in-2022-now-face-council-demolition-order-after-planning-row-over-basement-and-green-belt-rules/articleshow/133526561.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-couple-built-a-four-bedroom-home-in-wiltshire-for-their-disabled-daughter-in-2022-now-face-council-demolition-order-after-planning-row-over-basement-and-green-belt-rules/articleshow/133526561.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T04:02:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133526569,imgsize-173247.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[15 newborns killed in fire at Islamabad hospital's gynaecology ward in Pakistan]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/15-newborns-killed-in-fire-at-islamabad-hospitals-gynaecology-ward-in-pakistan/articleshow/133528725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/15-newborns-killed-in-fire-at-islamabad-hospitals-gynaecology-ward-in-pakistan/articleshow/133528725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T09:15:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133528887,imgsize-120908.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US halts visa appointments globally amid Trump's immigration crackdown]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133527702.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[United States visa appointments are paused worldwide for consular officer training. This initiative supports the administration's broader immigration enforcement efforts. Immigrant visa applicants are being notified of rescheduled interviews due to this program. The government is also tightening restrictions on legal immigration and visa issuances. These actions reflect ongoing reviews and adjustments to the US visa system.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-halts-visa-appointments-globally-amid-donald-trumps-immigration-crackdown/articleshow/133527702.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-halts-visa-appointments-globally-amid-donald-trumps-immigration-crackdown/articleshow/133527702.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T08:11:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133527841,imgsize-839014.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Singapore sends 70 tonnes of unwanted clothes to Malaysia to recycle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133523461.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Singapore sends up to seventy tonnes of clothing weekly to Malaysia for recycling. This cross-border initiative gives discarded garments a second life through reuse and repurposing. The volume has doubled in two years, highlighting the growing scale of textile waste management. At the Malaysian facility, clothes are sorted for resale or material recovery. This partnership aims to keep textiles in circulation and reduce landfill disposal.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-sends-70-tonnes-of-unwanted-clothes-to-malaysia-every-week-in-major-textile-recycling-partnership/articleshow/133523461.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-sends-70-tonnes-of-unwanted-clothes-to-malaysia-every-week-in-major-textile-recycling-partnership/articleshow/133523461.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T09:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133523620,imgsize-260510.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Port Houston donates $500,000 to 32 nonprofits for community programmes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133522668.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant move to bolster local communities, Port Houston has allocated $500,000 among 32 organizations focused on enhancing workforce training, educational resources, and health initiatives. A noteworthy portion of this funding is devoted to developing maritime career opportunities. Starting in 2027, upcoming grants will be aligned with the strategic Anchored in Action plan, reinforcing community development along the Houston Ship Channel region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/port-houston-donates-500000-to-32-nonprofits-supporting-workforce-training-stem-education-and-community-projects/articleshow/133522668.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/port-houston-donates-500000-to-32-nonprofits-supporting-workforce-training-stem-education-and-community-projects/articleshow/133522668.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T07:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133522895,imgsize-1597695.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Warned by FBI, Canadian police of credible plot': Pannun claims fresh threat to life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133527162.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/warned-by-fbi-canadian-police-of-credible-plot-sfjs-pannun-claims-fresh-threat-to-life/articleshow/133527162.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/warned-by-fbi-canadian-police-of-credible-plot-sfjs-pannun-claims-fresh-threat-to-life/articleshow/133527162.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T07:42:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133527162,imgsize-69280.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2022, CaseOh was mowing lawns for work; two years later, he won Content Creator of the Year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133501285.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[CaseOh’s creator journey moved at a ridiculous speed. In 2022, Case Dylan Baker was doing maintenance work with his father in rural Arkansas while making NBA 2K TikToks after work. His clips soon brought thousands of followers and pushed him onto Twitch. By December 2024, he had beaten several major creators to win Content Creator of the Year at The Game Awards.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com